error[E0401]: `h` holds a resource (`File`), so it must be used exactly once, but `close_twice` may use it more than once
  --> own_moot.ck:44:16
   |
44 |     apply f $ \h ->
   |                ^
   = help: a resource can't be copied: each operation on it gives back the one to use next, `let (x, f) = op f`

error[E0358]: `own` on `Int`, which holds no resource
  --> own_moot.ck:48:29
   |
48 | fn on_int f -> r : f~(v~own Int -> Int), r~Int
   |                             ^^^ `own` has no use here
   = help: `own` is for generic parameters that may receive a resource, as in `v~own a`; remove it

warning[W010]: `own` is implied: `File` holds a resource
  --> own_moot.ck:51:30
   |
51 | fn on_file f -> r : f~(v~own File -> Unit), r~Unit
   |                              ^^^^ this `own` can go
   = help: remove `own`; a resource is used exactly once anyway

own_moot.ck: 2 errors, 1 warning
